# nCr.fw — combinations (binomial coefficient): unordered k-subsets of n items.
#
#   nCr(n, k) = n! / (k! * (n-k)!)
#
# Authored as the MULTIPLICATIVE product form, NOT a ratio of big factorials:
#
#   product((n-k+i)/i, i in [1..k])
#     = ((n-k+1)/1) * ((n-k+2)/2) * ... * (n/k)
#
# Each partial product is itself an integer (a binomial coefficient), so the
# running value never exceeds the final answer — overflow-safe. fwiz carries
# the division exactly (structural rationals), so the result is exact even at
# the large end: nCr(54, 27) = 1946939425648112 to the last digit.
#
# nCr(n, 0) = 1 via the empty-product identity.
#
# Usage:
#   ./bin/fwiz 'stdlib/combinatorics/nCr(52, 5)'          # positional -> 2598960
#   nCr(n=52, k=5, result=?c)                              # named binding

[nCr(n, k) -> result]
result = product((n-k+i)/i, i in [1..k])
